  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "pct-01-meaning-conversions-mental-benchmarks",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Percentage Meaning, Conversions, and Mental Benchmarks",
    "description": "Understand percent as “per hundred” and move fluently among percentages, fractions, decimals, and simple percentage-of quantities.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start with a 100-piece whole so “percent” has a visible meaning. Move from exact conversions to mental benchmark fractions, then use those benchmarks for quick percentage-of calculations. Every practice item asks the learner to identify the same whole before converting.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 27,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 11, Percentage. Approved scope: Teach percent as parts per hundred, then convert percent to fraction and decimal and convert fractions/decimals back to percent. Include percentages below 1% and above 100%, mixed-number percentages, and comparison of quantities written in different forms. Build mental benchmarks such as 50%=1/2, 25%=1/4, 20%=1/5, 10%=1/10, 5%=1/20 and 1%=1/100. Explain that “of” means multiply and use these benchmarks to evaluate simple percentages mentally before relying on the x/100 rule. Learners should always identify what one whole or 100% represents."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's make percentages feel concrete.\n\nImagine a box with 100 equal tiles. If 37 tiles are marked, then 37 out of 100 are marked. That is exactly what 37% means.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Percent means “per hundred.”\n\n37% = 37/100.\n\nThe % sign is a shortcut for dividing by 100.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So 8% = 8/100 = 2/25.\n\nTo turn a percentage into a fraction, remove the % sign, divide by 100, then simplify.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
